# Session handoff

The first action of every session, before planning or editing, is to read `docs/context/NOW.md` (latest changes).

Then follow `AGENTS.md`. Protocol: `docs/context/HANDOFF.md`.

Do not edit code until `NOW.md` has been read.

When a stage changes code or decisions, or the user asks to hand off, update `NOW.md` before stopping: what changed, what is left, the next step. Keep it short. Do not mirror `NOW.md` to Obsidian.

`CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md` stay short pointers. Do not paste `AGENTS.md` back into them. `.cursorrules` stays the same text as `AGENTS.md`.

Commit only when the user asks.
